<resources><style name="Theme.Aiwa" parent="android:style/Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar"><item name="android:fontFamily">sans</item></style>
<!-- Reported live: DictateActivity's raw Theme.Translucent.NoTitleBar
     still showed a brief flash of Aiwa's own app icon/window on the
     FIRST tap of the widget's mic (Android's normal cold-start
     "preview window" for a process that isn't already resident in
     memory yet) — later taps, with the process already warm, were
     instant. windowDisablePreview tells the system not to show that
     placeholder window at all, and windowAnimationStyle=@null removes
     the transition animation on top of it. This can reduce but not
     fully erase the real, unavoidable cost of an Android process cold
     start itself — that part isn't a theme setting. -->
<style name="Theme.Dictate" parent="android:style/Theme.Translucent.NoTitleBar"><item name="android:windowDisablePreview">true</item><item name="android:windowAnimationStyle">@null</item></style></resources>
